<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n90026" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσρέω</span></b> , aor.
		
			Pass.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσερρύην</span> (v. infr.), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>flow towards a point, stream in,
				assemble</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.62
			</span></i>; <i>steal</i> or <i>creep towards</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινὸς προσρυέντος τῇ τραπέζῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.760a
				</span></i>
			; also, <i>rush up to</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐτῷ προσρυεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Brut.</u>
					16
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Parth.
				7.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Am.</u>
				8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>VS</u>
				2.30
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Med.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅταν γυνὴ κύουσα προσρέηται</span>
			<i>has losses</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Superf.</u>
				42
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
